  "source": {
    "generator": null,
    "notes": "Worst-of Asian call on two correlated assets, priced by path Monte Carlo. Demonstrates CORRELATED PROCESS SHOCKS (basket scope Phase 3): each stochastic_process declares a `correlations` field, so the per-step GBM shocks of the group are Cholesky-correlated every step and the whole PATHS co-move -- required here because the payoff depends on running averages (not single terminal draws). P1/P2 are correlated at rho=0.5; running averages avg1/avg2 are filter means (gap #2); the payoff is disc*max(min(avg1,avg2)-K,0). No closed form; validated structurally (worst-of <= each single-asset Asian) and by the realized path correlation (see engine/tests/correlated_processes_v2.rs). See CORRELATED_PROCESSES_EXAMPLE.md."
  },
